SUMMARY:The Body in the Room: Using Somatic Awareness in Clinical Practice
DESCRIPTION:Your clients’ bodies are speaking in every session—are you listening?\n\nJoin Karen Carnabucci\, LCSW\, TEP for a dynamic\, experiential training designed for licensed clinicians. This 3-hour workshop explores the somatic signals\, relational cues\, and nervous system data that often go unspoken in clinical work.\n\nGrounded\, practical\, and accessible—no prior somatic experience required.\n\n✨ You’ll learn how to:\n• Use your own body as a source of clinical insight\n• Track your client’s nervous system state with more ease\n• Integrate somatic awareness into any clinical orientation\n• Apply a body-forward lens in case consultation\n\nWalk away with tools you can start using right away in your sessions.\n\n🗓 Friday\, May 1\, 2026\n⏰ 9:00 AM – 12:00 PM\n📍 Inspire Wellness Collective | Lancaster\, PA\n💲 $45 | 3 CE Credits (includes psychodrama credits)\n🎟 Register now—limited spots available \n            \n        \n                \n            \n                \n                \n    Buy Tickets
URL:https://figlancaster.com/event/the-body-in-the-room-using-somatic-awareness-in-clinical-practice/
LOCATION:Inspire Wellness Collective\, 226 N. Arch Street\, Lancaster\, 17603
CATEGORIES:Education & Classes
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://fig.guide/content/uploads/sites/3/2026/04/body-in-the-room_orig.avif
ORGANIZER;CN="Inspire Wellness Collective":MAILTO:hello@inspirewellco.com
END:VEVENT
